WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
In 1775, doctor William Withering was
asked about a family remedy for dropsy:

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.880
swollen legs and breathlessness.

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.740
The brew held twenty or more herbs.

4
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.280
He reasoned that one mattered: foxglove.

5
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.900
Too much caused nausea,
vomiting and a very slow pulse.

6
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.580
He kept notes on 163 cases.

7
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.440
So how do we now test whether
a medicine really works?

8
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.720
In this mission, you'll follow
a new drug from lab cells,

9
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.320
through animal tests, to
its first trials in people.

10
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.210
Then you'll judge a
trial of 1200 patients,

11
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.980
and decide what its numbers really show.

12
00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:45.560
Your mission: find out how we test
whether a new medicine really works.
